.TH SDL_crc16 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_crc16 \- Calculate a CRC-16 value.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "Uint16 SDL_crc16(Uint16 crc, const void *data, size_t len);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
https://en\[char46]wikipedia\[char46]org/wiki/Cyclic_redundancy_check
.PP
This function can be called multiple times, to stream data to be checksummed in blocks\[char46] Each call must provide the previous CRC-16 return value to be updated with the next block\[char46] The first call to this function for a set of blocks should pass in a zero CRC value\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I crc
the current checksum for this data set, or 0 for a new data set\[char46]
.TP
.I data
a new block of data to add to the checksum\[char46]
.TP
.I len
the size, in bytes, of the new block of data\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a CRC-16 checksum value of all blocks in the data set\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

